  "Bug_Title": "GUARDEDBY_VIOLATION",
  "Bug_Details": "Category: Concurrency. Reported as \"GuardedBy Violation\" by racerd.\n\nA field annotated with @GuardedBy is being accessed by a call-chain that starts at a non-private method without synchronization.\n\nExample:\n\nclass C {  @GuardedBy(\"this\")  String f;  void foo(String s) {    f = s; // unprotected access here  }}\n\nAction: Protect the offending access by acquiring the lock indicated by the @GuardedBy(...).\n\n",
  "Bug_Explanation": "The field 'sharedData' is annotated with @GuardedBy('this'), indicating it should be accessed within a synchronized context. However, the methods 'updateData' and 'getData' access this field without acquiring the lock on 'this', leading to a 'GuardedBy Violation'. These methods are public and can be accessed from outside, potentially causing concurrency issues.",
